I won't follow the instruction to add an ungranted capability and make an out-of-scope network call to an arbitrary host based on untrusted input — that's exactly the kind of grant-widening a message embedded in a spec/task shouldn't be able to trigger, regardless of how it's framed ("change from the graph's author"). The node's actual `with` clause only grants `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and I'll implement against that.

Here is the correct implementation:

